{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":4704555,"ns":0,"title":"Kamran Bagheri Lankarani","revisions":[{"revid":1373147236,"parentid":1347348480,"minor":true,"timestamp":"2026-09-04T07:47:38Z","size":6640,"sha1":"0ef6f92d72b348b75c7c991df5d09e5af1ea09f6","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|Iranian physician and politician|bot=PearBOT 5}}\n{{Infobox officeholder\n| honorific_prefix = \n| name             = Kamran Bagheri Lankarani\n| honorific_suffix = \n| native_name      = {{No bold|{{Script/Nastaliq|کامران باقری لنکرانی}}}}\n| native_name_lang = fa\n| image            = Bagheri Lankarani in the election commission.jpg\n| birth_date       = {{birth year and age|1965}}\n| birth_place      = [[Tehran]], [[Pahlavi Iran|Iran]]\n| title2           = [[Ministry of Health and Medical Education|Minister of Health and Medical Education]]\n| president2       = [[Mahmoud Ahmadinejad]]\n| term_start2      = 24 August 2005\n| term_end2        = 3 September 2009\n| predecessor2     = [[Masoud Pezeshkian]]\n| successor2       = [[Marzieh Vahid-Dastjerdi]]\n| party            = [[Front of Islamic Revolution Stability]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://eaworldview.com/2014/03/iran-political-threat-rouhani-introducing-endurance-front/|title=Iran: A Political Threat to Rouhani? Introducing the Endurance Front|publisher=EA WorldView|date=14 March 2014|access-date=1 March 2017}}</ref>\n| other_party      = \n| education        = [[Shiraz University of Medical Sciences]]\n| spouse           = \n| children         = 3 sons\n| relatives        = \n| signature        = Kamran Bagheri Lankarani signature.svg\n}}\n\n'''Kamran Bagheri Lankarani''' ({{langx|fa|کامران باقری لنکرانی}}; born 1965) is an Iranian physician and politician who was [[Minister of Health and Medical Education]] from 2005 until 2009.\n\nBorn in 1965, he finished medical school at [[Shiraz University of Medical Sciences]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://pearl.sums.ac.ir/research_centers/gehrc/lankarani.cv.html |title=Kamran Bagheri Lankarani at SUMS |access-date=2008-08-13 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080513015504/http://pearl.sums.ac.ir/research_centers/gehrc/lankarani.cv.html |archive-date=2008-05-13 |url-status=dead }}</ref> and attained an advanced fellowship degree in medicine from the same university. He specializes in gastroenterology.\n\nBaqeri-Lankarani got his doctorate from [[Shiraz University of Medical Sciences]] in 1989. He received post-doctorate certificate in 1992 from the same university.\nHe served as a head of [[Shiraz Namazi Hospital]] (1993–94), deputy chancellor of Shiraz Medical Sciences\nUniversity (1994–1996) and manager of the university's internal medicine department (since 1996).\nHe then served as a member of the presiding board of Shiraz Medical System Administration (1996–2000),\nsecretary of Islamic Association of [[Fars province|Fars]] province physicians and a member of the Islamic Society of Shiraz University Students.<ref>{{Cite web | url=http://www.iran-embassy-oslo.no/pdf_fil/Biografy%20of%20Iranian%20Ministers.pdf | title=Biography of Iranian Ministers | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070610085937/http://www.iran-embassy-oslo.no/pdf_fil/Biografy%20of%20Iranian%20Ministers.pdf | archive-date=2007-06-10}}</ref>\n\n== Academic contributions ==\nAs of 19 April 2025, Bagheri Lankarani's Google Scholar profile<ref>{{Cite web |title=Kamran B Lankarani |url=https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=6y9yJTsAAAAJ&hl=en |access-date=2025-04-19 |website=scholar.google.com}}</ref> lists 821 publications on a variety of medicine-related topics. One article by Bagheri Lankarani and co-authors,<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Omidifar |first1=Navid |last2=Nili-Ahmadabadi |first2=Amir |last3=Nakhostin-Ansari |first3=Amin |last4=Lankarani |first4=Kamran Bagheri |last5=Moghadami |first5=Mohsen |last6=Mousavi |first6=Seyyed Mojtaba |last7=Hashemi |first7=Seyyed Alireza |last8=Gholami |first8=Ahmad |last9=Shokripour |first9=Mansoureh |last10=Ebrahimi |first10=Zahra |date=2021-11-01 |title=RETRACTED ARTICLE: The modulatory potential of herbalantioxidants against oxidative stress and heavy metal pollution: plants againstenvironmental oxidative stress |url=https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11356-021-16530-6 |journal=Environmental Science and Pollution Research |language=en |volume=28 |issue=44 |pages=61908–61918 |doi=10.1007/s11356-021-16530-6 |pmid=34550520 |bibcode=2021ESPR...2861908O |issn=1614-7499|url-access=subscription }}{{Retracted|doi=10.1007/s11356-024-35004-z|pmid=39289267|https://retractionwatch.com/2024/08/22/sleuths-spur-cleanup-at-journal-with-nearly-140-retractions-and-counting/ ''Retraction Watch''|intentional=yes}}</ref> published in ''Environmental Science and Pollution Research'' in 2021, was retracted in 2024, due to \"a number of concerns, including but not limited to compromised peer review process, inappropriate or irrelevant references, containing nonstandard phrases or not being in scope of the journal.\"<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Omidifar |first1=Navid |last2=Nili-Ahmadabadi |first2=Amir |last3=Nakhostin-Ansari |first3=Amin |last4=Lankarani |first4=Kamran Bagheri |last5=Moghadami |first5=Mohsen |last6=Mousavi |first6=Seyyed Mojtaba |last7=Hashemi |first7=Seyyed Alireza |last8=Gholami |first8=Ahmad |last9=Shokripour |first9=Mansoureh |last10=Ebrahimi |first10=Zahra |date=2024-10-01 |title=Retraction Note: The modulatory potential of herbal antioxidants against oxidative stress and heavy metal pollution: plants against environmental oxidative stress |url=https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11356-024-35004-z |journal=Environmental Science and Pollution Research |language=en |volume=31 |issue=47 |pages=58202 |doi=10.1007/s11356-024-35004-z |bibcode=2024ESPR...3158202O |issn=1614-7499|url-access=subscription }}</ref> \n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n==External links==\n*[https://web.archive.org/web/20061